    "summary": "Carrier Dome ’82 delivers soaring leads, funk‑tight grooves and a stellar Playing > Crazy Fingers.",
    "review": "The September‑24, 1982 night at Syracuse’s Carrier Dome captures the Dead in full swing during their high‑octane Autumn ’82 tour. The band launches into a crisp set that builds to a spectacular second‑set opener – a seamless segue from “Playing In The Band” straight into an incendiary “Crazy Fingers,” where Jerry’s guitar soars with grand, growling leads and Brent’s electric piano adds bright texture on “Far From Me.” Phil’s bass bubbles with massive bombs throughout the jams, while Bill and Mickey lock down a funky, tight groove that drives the after‑drums jam to a thunderous climax. Bob Weir’s stage antics during “Sugar Magnolia” inject extra visual excitement, and the medley of “Iko Iko → Truckin’ → Goin’ Down The Road Feeling Bad → Black Peter → Around & Around” showcases the band’s improvisational flow at its most inspired. A standout moment is the debut‑era energy on “Throwing Stones,” hinting at the new material that would define the era, all captured with crystal‑clear clarity in the recommended soundboard source.",
